{"answer":"### Bacterial Cell Structure\n\n```text\n      +-------------------------------------------------------+\n      |                  Capsule (Outer layer)                |\n      |   +-----------------------------------------------+   |\n      |   |               Cell Wall                       |   |\n      |   |   +---------------------------------------+   |   |\n      |   |   |   Plasma Membrane                     |   |   |\n      |   |   |   +-------------------------------+   |   |   |\n      |   |   |   | Cytoplasm, Ribosomes,         |   |   |   |\n      |   |   |   | Nucleoid (Circular DNA)       |   |   |   |\n      |   |   |   +-------------------------------+   |   |   |\n      |   |   +---------------------------------------+   |   |\n      |   +-----------------------------------------------+   |\n      +-------------------------------------------------------+\n                  (Flagellum --->)  ~~~~~~~~~~\n                  (Pili ------->)   -----\n```\n\n**Key components:** Capsule, Cell wall, Plasma membrane, Cytoplasm, Nucleoid (DNA), Ribosomes, Flagella, and Pili.","proTip":"Keep bacterial diagram sketches simple, labeling at least the capsule, cell wall, flagellum, and nucleoid region.","videoLinks":[{"title":"Bacterial cell structure diagram easy","url":"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Bacterial+cell+structure+diagram+easy"},{"title":"Prokaryotic cell structure","url":"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Prokaryotic+cell+structure"}]}